-- The same hazard one level down: `Syntax.Codec` lives in the standard
-- library, and a source directory root is searched before the embedded
-- standard library, so a file at this path shadows it for anything resolving
-- against the target's search path. The shadow decodes its input artifacts
-- through this module, so a target that supplied it could decide what the
-- checker believes it was given.

fn decode_surface(text : String) : String = ""

fn codec_error_message(text : String) : String = text
